{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Progress (lane 04f1, worktree epic-04f1-facade at 2e28d817a7e): implemented on the plan as reviewed, with these decisions and deviations.\n\n1. `_mcp_schema.OUTPUT_SCHEMAS_BY_TOOL` covers 52 tools. `inline_schema` hoists common `$defs` transitively and REFUSES any other cross-file `$ref` (ValueError at startup) rather than leaving one unresolved. The installer asserts `output_model is not None` and `wrap_output == (kind != \"object\")` per tool.\n2. `render_workflow` still advertises FastMCP's auto `{\"result\": string}` schema (it returns a plain string); it is the one EXEMPT_GENERIC entry left, and the canonical test excludes it by name. `list_tools()` = 64, 11 without outputSchema (AC 4).\n3. Input entries: `rebar.types.FileImpactEntry`/`VerifyCommandEntry` are `typing.TypedDict`, which pydantic refuses on Python 3.11 (CI tests 3.11). `_mcp_schema.pydantic_typed_dict` rebuilds them as `typing_extensions.TypedDict` (same keys, required set, docstring); verified in a 3.11 venv. `_mcp_writes` falls back to the plain TypedDict on a core-only install (no `typing_extensions`), pinned by a rewritten test in `test_mcp.py` (the old pydantic-absent model-placeholder test had nothing left to test).\n4. Finding: the store's `set_file_impact`/`set_verify_commands` validator (`_commands/leaf.py:229-252`) requires string `reason` / `dd_id` / `dd_text` on every entry, while `common.schema.json` marks them optional. Unchanged behaviour (the old `_dump` dropped None and the store then refused too). So `test_set_file_impact_accepts_typed_entries` sends `{\"path\",\"reason\"}` and asserts `reason: null` is refused at the transport; the release note says the store still requires the keys.\n5. Removing the mirror's null re-adds shrank list rows: `test_mcp_list_read_surface.py` drops the \"model defaults\" budget axis (250-row case now 105,292 wire bytes, was 135,902; still over the 90,000 budget, so the refusal test still bites), and `test_ready_default_is_narrower...` now asserts the exact summary key set instead of a length comparison that only held because the mirror padded list rows.\n6. `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_js_safe_integers.py` walks advertised outputSchemas for ns-timestamp fields instead of model fields.\n7. Out-of-plan files touched: `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py` (drop `dump=ms._dump`; the script is deleted by the next story), `tests/unit/test_gen_mcp_reference.py`, `tests/unit/test_review_lifecycle_docs.py`, `tests/unit/test_bridge_projects_surfaces_heldout.py`, `tests/unit/test_ticket_project_fields.py` (fake ctx `dump=`), `tests/unit/test_read_freshness_parity.py` (dict row access), `tests/interfaces/facades/test_file_impact_scope_heldout.py` (ack key absent, not null), `src/rebar/types.py` new `PushStatus` (generated). File impact will be widened before close.\nlint and typecheck green; make verify running."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792384807893111001,"uuid":"e30e4b5b-2edf-49db-a8a6-559fd664e558"}